1 OCCU Electrician
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Immigrated to the US in 1885 according to the 1900 census records.  Family stories repeated by Charles' children and grandchildren is that he came to the US with a cousin, Gus Lindbergh.  The story has it that Axel
2 CONC  Branzell and Charles August "Gus" Lindbergh (1859-1924) were first cousins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles attended General Electric School of Electricity in Schenectady, NY, before marrying Emma.  The years of attendance are unknown.  Charles is shown as being a laborer on the census records.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles resided in Ironwood, Michigan, at the time of his marriage to Emma.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles and Emma were married at a Swedish Lutheran ceremny.  Billy was baptized at Emma's mother's home.  Charles beleived in reincarnation and was an athiest according to family stories told by Walter.  Emma's brother, Oscar, an
2 CONC d P. E. Peterson witnessed the marriage between Charles and Emma.  Two theories of who P. E. Peterson is:  (1) a neighbor; (2) Emma's brother Ernest.
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried Forest Lawn Cemetary, Detroit, MI, Lots 8 SE 1/4, No. 135, Section 2 and Lot 7 SE 1/2. . .
