1 NAME Gustaf Erhard /Schützer/
2 GIVN Gustaf Erhard
2 SURN Schützer
2 _MARNM Schützer
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 JUL 1732
2 PLAC Niedersachsen
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hameln-Pyrmont
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 JUL 1813
2 PLAC Kålsheden
2 ADDR
3 CITY Långserud
3 STAE Värmlands län
3 CTRY Sverige
1 OCCU Fältväbel 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Schützer family - the Lingserud part.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to unconfirmed notes, Gustaf Erhard Schützer was born in Hameln, Hannover in Germany 1732. (He may have lived in Austria). It is confirmed that he and his wife madame Elisabeth von Kiessel lived in Södra Ny 1755 when the
2 CONC ir first son Carl magnus was born march 17:th. The church books of Södra Ny say that they came from Gothenburg but not which part of the city they lived in before moving to Varmland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Södra Ny Carl Fredrik was born 1757 and Anna Catarina 1760. The family then moved to Grava where the son Magnus Gabriel was born 14:th of September 1763 and Sara Christina 5:th of march 1767. At the time when they moved Carl Ma
2 CONC gnus was not in the church books so he probably died as a young child in Södra Ny. (He is not found in the "death books" for Södra Ny or Grava. After 1767 the family moved to Långserud where the last three children were born, Chri
2 CONC stian Erhard 25:th of august 1769, Sven 1770 (date unknown) and Gustaf Fredrik 27:th of June 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth von Kiessel died October 19:th 1788 and Gustaf Erhard remarried with Cajsa Svensdotter and moved to Norra Rada where Elisabeth Sofia was born September 5:th 1795 and Nils may 30:th 1798. Nils called himself Gustafsson an
2 CONC d according to the church books he "disappeared". Elisabeth Sofia is not checked in the church books. Of the children in the first marriage only three had family and children and they lived in different places.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Erhard born 1769 moved to Norra Radar and founded the "Norra Radar- part" of the family tree which is very difficult to do research for since the name "Schützer" disappeared in the middle of the 19:th century when the so
2 CONC n Per died and the children called themselves Persson or Persdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sven, born 1770, stayed in Lingserud and founded the "LÅNGSERUD-part".
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustaf Fredrik, born 1774, also moved to Norra Radar and then to Alga. He started the "@gi part" of the family tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Alga-part and the Lingserud-part of the family have been subject to a lot of research. I belong to the LÅNGSERUD part and have many hundreds of pages with my family tree. You can look at it when you come. Sven's grandson Augus
2 CONC t Schützer and his wife Agneta Svensdotter had 9 children and from there the family history is complete.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the papers you can see that Gustaf Erhard died July 7:th 1813 in Långserud but you probably know that already. Elisabeth von Kiessel's parents were "Cornett" Magnus Adolf von Kiessel and Sara Beata Vigelia. (Cornett is a milita
2 CONC ry grade = lieutenant (how the h.. do you spell it???) in US Army according to my father-in-law who was a colonel in the Swedish army). Gustaf Erhard's son Carl Fredrik was taken prisoner in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sven Schützer, born 1770, drowned in Kolsheden, Lingserud April 21:st 1836. He was a "battalion drummer" (I don't know if that's what you call it - I'm writing this in our farmhouse in Sunne and have no English dictionary).
2 CONT
2 CONT Olof Schützer, born 1810, was a drummer and died February 28:th 1898 in Ristaka, Lågserud. His daughter Klara, born 1849, moved to Tönsberg, Norway 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/h/e/n/Albert-W-Henderson/index.html "Looking for decendents of Gustaf Erhard Schützer. He was born in 1732, either in Hameln, Hannover, Germany, or possibly Austria. He and his wife, Mada
2 CONC me Elisabeth von Kiessel, lived in Södra Ny, Sweden, in 1755. There first son, Carl magnus, was born there on March 17 of that year. The church books of Södra Ny say that they came from Gothenburg before moving to Värmland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some members of the Schützer clan moved to Norway. From there, some moved to the United States. Others left directly from Sweden for America. Some are accounted for, others are not. The name has various spellings: Schuster, Schost
2 CONC er, Schutzer -- with or without dots -- even Schützercrantz (indicating nobility). And some branches changed the name entirely, preferring to use, for example, the patronymic Jansson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Currently we are looking for Beda and Emma Schützer. They, along with Anna Sofia Schützers and her younger brother, Johan Fredrik Schützer (AKA Jansson), were the children of Andreas Jansson Schützer and Stina Casja Andersson. Ann
2 CONC a was born February 2, 1872, in Segerfores, Arvika, Sweden. We think Beda was born November 15, 1874, and Johan was probably a decade younger than Anna. At some point, the family moved from Värmland to a farm, known as Bjørkemoen,
2 CONC  just outside of Oslo. Anna left for the United States from the Port of Oslo on March 31, 1893. She married G. Albert Henderson (also known as Gustaf Albert Hendersson), had two children and died in Chicago May 29, 1936. Their son
2 CONC , Albert, had three children. Johan married a Norwegian woman, Josephine O. Lear. They, along with two children, came to the United States in 1903, and settled in San Francisco, where they had four more children. None of the male 
2 CONC offspring had male children, and so the name has died out.
2 CONT
2 CONT Several other members of the Schützer clan have surfaced, but we haven't been able to trace their whereabouts or the whereabouts of their decendents since leaving Scandinavia. They include: Schützer, Estrid, 24, from Ljusne, left 
2 CONC in 1925, for Chicago; Schützer, Joh. A 33, from Långserud, who left in 1901, for Kane (which may be the Kane in Pennsylvania), and someone by the name of Schützer, Wilhelmin, 26, who might have been his wife. "
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
