1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emigrated to North America in 1887. Left from Kristiania (Oslo) with the skip Angelo on the 11 March 1887 and arrived to NY with the skip SS Alaska from Liverpool/Queenstown on the 28 March 1887 (New York Passenger
2 CONC  List 1820-1897: M237 Roll 504, page 889). He seemed to have bought some property in North Dakota in December 1902 (160 acres in Walsh county, Grand Forke) and asked for pre-emption in Saskatchewan, Canada, in December 1902 and Ju
2 CONC ly 1907 but he never bought the properties in Saskatchewan. According to the files, they where both cancelled. In January 1910 he asked for a pre-emption to buy  property in Alberta, Canada, (Goddard) and he receives the property 
2 CONC in 1913. Registered in Alberta in the Canadian Census 1911.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was was registered as lodger in Lethbridge, Burlington, Alberta (at farmer Charles Swanson), in 1916 but working on own account. In 1921 he was registered at the same property but as head.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the registration for voting in 1935 he was registered at Lucky Strike, Alberta. He probably died in Ponoka, Alberta, 22 December 1946, in the age of 77. He seems to have been singe all his life.
